{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"0000000000000004","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 at\n\n**情緒觸發點／能力著力點**\n\nsurprised at · shocked at · amazed at · good at · bad at · aim at · laugh at","x":705,"y":20,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0000000000000005","type":"text","text":"## Q2：是不是在描述『依附在表面上』？\n\n依賴、依據、聚焦的關係","x":0,"y":550,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000007","type":"text","text":"## Q3：是不是在描述『在容器/範圍內』？\n\n某種狀態、投入的領域","x":0,"y":1100,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000009","type":"text","text":"## Q4：是不是在描述『構成、來源』？\n\n某事物由什麼組成，或感受的來源","x":0,"y":1650,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"000000000000000b","type":"text","text":"## Q5：是不是在描述『起點、分離』？\n\n來源、區別，或阻止某事發生","x":0,"y":2200,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"000000000000000d","type":"text","text":"## Q6：是不是在描述『兩者之間的關係』？\n\n方向性、連結、比較，或針對某人的態度/互動/對抗","x":0,"y":2750,"width":450,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"000000000000001d","type":"text","text":"## Q7：是不是在描述『目的、交換、責任、理由、代表』？","x":0,"y":4750,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000021","type":"text","text":"## Q8：是不是牽涉『支配、反覆鑽研、因某事起爭執、克服跨越，或時間跨度』？\n\n（over 的語意較零散，不是單一語意軸）","x":0,"y":5350,"width":450,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000003","type":"text","text":"## Q1：這是不是在描述『指向一個點/觸發點』？\n\n情緒瞬間被引爆的點、能力施力的著力點","x":0,"y":20,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"000000000000002b","type":"text","text":"## Q9：是不是在描述『被動語態中動作的施者、方式或媒介』？\n\n動作是被誰做的、透過什麼方式/工具完成的","x":0,"y":5950,"width":450,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000023","type":"text","text":"#### 支配／控制\n\npreside over · rule over · have control/authority over · triumph over","x":1610,"y":5750,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0000000000000027","type":"text","text":"#### 時間或活動跨度\n\nover the years · over dinner","x":1610,"y":6120,"width":460,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0000000000000024","type":"text","text":"#### 反覆思考／鑽研\n\nthink/mull/ponder over · pore over · puzzle over · brood/agonize over","x":1610,"y":6480,"width":460,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0000000000000001","type":"text","text":"# ⚠️ 使用前提\n\n這棵樹只能覆蓋『語意類別可以推導』的搭配傾向，不是絕對規則。\n\n以下狀況推不出來，要查字典或個別記憶：\n- 同字換介係詞換意思（agree with/on/to、talk to/with、look at/for/after/into）\n- 英式/美式差異（different from/to vs than）\n- 純約定俗成、字面已脫鉤的片語動詞（look up、give up、come across）\n- 及物性決定要不要介係詞（supervise vs preside over）\n- 特定句型（make it adj for sb to do sth）\n\n詳見完整規律筆記的規律二、三、四、五、七。","x":-100,"y":-960,"width":650,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"0000000000000030","type":"text","text":"## Q0：這個字是不是拉丁/希臘字根＋前綴構成的學術動詞？能不能看出字根意象？\n\n例：persist = per-（貫穿）+ sistere、insist = in-（壓向）+ sistere","x":0,"y":-560,"width":450,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000020","type":"text","text":"#### ✅ 用 for（理由/代表）\n\n說明為什麼，或代替誰做某事\n\nresponsible for · known for · blame...for · thank sb for · apologize for · commend sb for","x":1610,"y":5040,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"000000000000001f","type":"text","text":"#### ✅ 用 for（尋求目標）\n\n動作朝向想得到的東西\n\nlook for · search for · hope for · apply for · ask for · wait for · pay for","x":1610,"y":4740,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0000000000000013","type":"text","text":"**Q（人）：這個特質不需要對方回應也成立嗎？**\n\n單向：即使對方毫無反應，特質依然存在","x":1260,"y":3900,"width":440,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000015","type":"text","text":"##### ✅ 用 with\n\n**互動/應對方式**（需要一來一往的交手過程才成立）\n\nangry with · annoyed with · patient with · gentle with · careful with · strict with · assertive with","x":1610,"y":4270,"width":460,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0000000000000016","type":"text","text":"**Q（事/情況）：是「事物對人顯現的性質」或「靜態比較關係」嗎？**\n\n人是接收端，或兩個事物在比較","x":2840,"y":3580,"width":460,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000018","type":"text","text":"**Q（事/情況）：這是你對這件事產生的情緒/滿足感嗎？**","x":3290,"y":3900,"width":440,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000029","type":"text","text":"##### ✅ 用 about\n\n**情緒/感受的原因（事/情況）——多數情緒字對事的預設選擇**\n\nangry about · annoyed about · disappointed about · upset about · happy about · excited about · sorry about","x":3730,"y":4270,"width":460,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0000000000000019","type":"text","text":"#### ⚠️ 例外：這些字不論對象是人是事都固定用 with\n\npleased with · satisfied with · disappointed with · bored with · fed up with · obsessed with\n\n不是語意可推導的分支，是規律六裡的個別記憶清單，不會像 angry/annoyed/disappointed/upset/happy/excited/sorry 那樣切換成 about。","x":3730,"y":4740,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"0000000000000012","type":"text","text":"##### ✅ 用 to\n\n**承諾/依附狀態**\n\nmarried to · engaged to · committed to · devoted to · dedicated to · addicted to · accustomed to · used to","x":380,"y":3900,"width":420,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"000000000000002a","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 between\n\n**比較/選擇/區分兩個並列項目（A and B），而不是單一方向性的關係**\n\ndifference between · choose between · distinguish between · decide between · relationship between · between you and me","x":705,"y":2750,"width":450,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"000000000000000e","type":"text","text":"### 有沒有『主動對抗／施力衝突』的動作感？","x":705,"y":3120,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"000000000000001b","type":"text","text":"#### ⚠️ 例外：familiar 會反轉方向\n\nI am familiar **with** this topic.（人主動，走 with）\nThis topic is familiar **to** me.（事物→人，同 obvious to 組，走 to）\n\n關鍵是誰當主詞，不是語意類別本身。","x":2320,"y":4740,"width":600,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"0000000000000011","type":"text","text":"**Q（人）：這是不是「承諾/依附的持續狀態」？**\n\n一旦達成就成為一種身份/狀態，不需對方持續回應。\n\n例：married, engaged, committed, devoted, dedicated, addicted, accustomed, used","x":705,"y":3580,"width":460,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000014","type":"text","text":"##### ✅ 用 to\n\n**單向態度/行為**\n\nkind to · rude to · polite to · cruel to · generous to · loyal to · friendly to · hostile to","x":705,"y":4270,"width":450,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"000000000000001e","type":"text","text":"### 是「尋求/爭取的目標」還是「理由/代表某人做某事」？","x":705,"y":4740,"width":450,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"000000000000000c","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 from\n\n**起點／區別／阻止**\n\nsuffer from · differ from · prevent...from · recover from · different from · separate from","x":705,"y":2200,"width":460,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"000000000000000a","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 of\n\n**構成／來源**\n\nconsist of · made of · afraid of · aware of · proud of · full of · capable of","x":705,"y":1650,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0000000000000008","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 in\n\n**狀態／投入的領域**\n\ninterested in · engaged in · believe in · succeed in · confident in · involved in · persist in","x":705,"y":1100,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0000000000000006","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 on\n\n**依賴／依據／聚焦**\n\ndepend on · rely on · base on · focus on · insist on · keen on","x":705,"y":550,"width":450,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0000000000000002","type":"file","file":"2.personal-notes/english-learning-notes/2.Collocation rules for verbs,adjectives followed by prepositions.md","x":705,"y":-960,"width":450,"height":260},
		{
			"id":"ddfb83772cf733ef",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"![[4.Visual imagery method for understanding prepositions#方法一：拉丁/希臘字根學術動詞 → 查字根意象]]",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":705,
			"y":-560,
			"width":450,
			"height":260
		},
		{"id":"0000000000000026","type":"text","text":"#### 克服／越過障礙\n\nget over · take over","x":1610,"y":5350,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0000000000000017","type":"text","text":"##### ✅ 用 to\n\n**性質外顯／靜態比較**\n\nobvious to · clear to · similar to · related to · equal to · identical to · opposite to","x":2410,"y":3900,"width":420,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"000000000000001a","type":"text","text":"##### ✅ 用 with\n\n**熟悉/相容/主動涉入，或擁有配備**\n\nfamiliar with · compatible with · involved with · associated with · busy with · equipped with","x":2920,"y":4270,"width":460,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"000000000000000f","type":"text","text":"#### ✅ 用 against\n\n**對抗／逆著方向**（有主動抵抗/衝突施力）\n\nfight against · protect against · discriminate against · argue against · compare...against · lean against","x":1610,"y":2750,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0000000000000010","type":"text","text":"### 沒有對抗動作感 → 進入 to／with 判斷\n\n**Q：後面接的是「人」還是「事/情況」？**","x":1610,"y":3120,"width":460,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0000000000000025","type":"text","text":"#### 因某事引發爭執/情緒\n\nargue/fight/quarrel/dispute over · cry over · worry over","x":1610,"y":6810,"width":460,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0000000000000028","type":"text","text":"## 都不符合以上任何類別？\n\n這通常是規律二～五、七涵蓋的『特定字/句型』或純約定俗成搭配（如 look up、give up），核心意象推不出來。\n\n請查字典/語料庫（Ozdic、COCA）或個別記憶。","x":450,"y":6880,"width":450,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"000000000000002c","type":"text","text":"### ✅ 用 by\n\n**被動語態的施者／方式／媒介**\n\ncaused by · accompanied by · followed by · replaced by · surrounded by · characterized by · dominated by · affected by · influenced by · driven by\n\n⚠️ 部分觸發點類情緒字（surprised/shocked/amazed/impressed）by 和 at 可換用：by 強調造成的原因/施者，at 強調反應的觸發點。","x":-480,"y":6880,"width":480,"height":260,"color":"5"}
	],
